rL\u0000\u0007optionsq\u0000~\u0000\u000FL\u0000\u0007serversq\u0000~\u0000\u000FL\u0000\u000Bsubcategoryq\u0000~\u0000\rL\u0000\u0005topicq\u0000~\u0000\rL\u0000\u0004typeq\u0000~\u0000\rL\u0000\u0005unitsq\u0000~\u0000\rxp\u0000\u0000\u0000'\u0010sq\u0000~\u0000\u0003\u0000t\u0000\nInstrumentt\u0000\u00BAPaper Reference\:\nMcEwen, A. S., et al. (2007), Mars Reconnaissance Orbiter's High Resolution Imaging Science Experiment (HiRISE), J. Geophys. Res., 112, E05S02, doi\:10.1029/2005JE002605.t\u00038The High Resolution Imaging Science Experiment (HiRISE) camera offers unprecedented image quality, giving us a view of the Red Planet in a way never before seen.  It\u00E2\u0080\u0099s the most powerful camera ever to leave Earth\u00E2\u0080\u0099s orbit.  HiRISE offers three data sets, the Experiment Data Record (EDR) data set, the Reduce Data Record (RDR), and the Digital Terrain Model (DTM) data set. Full resolution HiRISE stamps are accurately projected data for use with other datasets such as CTX data.\n**************************************************\nNote\: The electronics unit for CCD RED4 started to fail in August 2023  and we have not been acquiring images in this central swath of the images.  The processing pipelines will be updated to fill this gap with the IR10 data  for some products. The 3-color coverage is now reduced in width.t\u0000\u0003721t\u0000\u0003allt\u0000\u001F,http\://hirise.lpl.arizona.edu,sr\u0000\u0010java.lang.Double\u0080\u00B3\u00C2J)k\u00FB\u0004\u0002\u0000\u0001D\u0000\u0005valuexq\u0000~\u0000\u0007?\u00F0\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000t\u0000\rHiRISE Stampssr\u0000\u0013java.util.ArrayListx\u0081\u00D2\u001D\u0099\u00C7a\u009D\u0003\u0000\u0001I\u0000\u0004sizexp\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0006w\u0004\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0006q\u0000~\u00008t\u0000\nproduct_idt\u0000\u001Cspacecraft_clock_start_countt\u0000\u000Fcenter_latitudet\u0000\nlocal_timet\u0000\u000Fspatial_summingxsq\u0000~\u0000E\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000w\u0004\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000xt\u0000\u0006HiRISEt\u0000\u0006HiRISEt\u0000\u0005stampt\u0000\u0000t\u0000\u0012HiRISE Full Stampsq\u0000~\u0000\u0018pq\u0000~\u0000,ppt\u0002\u00CFStampFetcher?limit\=2000000&instrument\=HiRISE_Full&viewArea\=50.464,-56.664,50.464,-56.664,50.464,-56.656,50.463,-56.648,50.463,-56.639,50.463,-56.631,50.463,-56.623,50.463,-56.614,50.463,-56.606,50.463,-56.598,50.463,-56.589,50.463,-56.581,50.463,-56.581,50.486,-56.581,50.510,-56.581,50.534,-56.581,50.558,-56.581,50.581,-56.580,50.605,-56.580,50.629,-56.580,50.653,-56.580,50.676,-56.580,50.700,-56.580,50.700,-56.588,50.701,-56.596,50.701,-56.605,50.701,-56.613,50.701,-56.621,50.701,-56.630,50.701,-56.638,50.702,-56.646,50.702,-56.655,50.702,-56.663,50.702,-56.663,50.678,-56.663,50.654,-56.663,50.630,-56.663,50.607,-56.664,50.583,-56.664,50.559,-56.664,50.535,-56.664,50.511,-56.664,50.487,-56.664,50.464,-56.664,sq\u0000~\u0000\u0003\u0000ppppur\u0000.[Ledu.asu.jmars.layer.stamp.FilledStamp$State;\u00BF]p@^l\u0090\u0097\u0002\u0000\u0000xp\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0001sr\u00004edu.asu.jmars.layer.stamp.FilledStampImageType$State\u00DE\u00BFaa\u0017\u0013\u0093\u00E9\u0002\u0000\u0001[\u0000\u0008colorMapt\u0000\u0002[Bxr\u0000+edu.asu.jmars.layer.stamp.FilledStamp$State\u00DE\u00BFaa\u0017\u0013\u0093\u00E9\u0002\u0000\u0003[\u0000\u0008colorMapq\u0000~\u0000WL\u0000\u0002idq\u0000~\u0000\rL\u0000\timageTypeq\u0000~\u0000\rxppt\u0000\u0013ESP_058971_1230_REDt\u0000\u000BHiRISE_FULLur\u0000\u0002[B\u00AC\u00F3\u0017\u00F8\u0006\u0008T\u00E0\u0002\u0000\u0000xp\u0000\u0000\u0000^\#cmap256  Colormap file, created by JMARS\n0\t0x000000\n255\t0xFFFFFF\ninterpolation lin_hsb_short\nq\u0000~\u0000,t\u0000\t3dEnabledsq\u0000~\u0000\u0003\u0000t\u0000\u0005alphasr\u0000\u000Fjava.lang.Float\u00DA\u00ED\u00C9\u00A2\u00DB<\u00F0\u00EC\u0002\u0000\u0001F\u0000\u0005valuexq\u0000~\u0000\u0007?\u0080\u0000\u0000t\u0000\u000BmainEnabledsq\u0000~\u0000\u0003\u0000t\u0000\u0006dockedsq\u0000~\u0000\u0003\u0000x
View2Overlay=false
